# Retail Sales & Profitability Analysis

## 1. Project Overview

This project investigates retail sales and profitability to identify business performance patterns, potential areas of concern, and opportunities for improvement.

The analysis uses the Sample Superstore dataset and focuses on turning transactional data into actionable business insights.

## 2. Business Problem

Retail businesses need to understand whether strong sales translate into sustainable profitability.

This project investigates product performance, regional differences, discount patterns, and changes in sales and profit over time to support better business decisions.

## 3. Objectives

- Assess the quality and reliability of the dataset.
- Clean and prepare the data for analysis.
- Analyze sales and profit across product categories, sub-categories, customers, and regions.
- Investigate the relationship between discounts and profitability.
- Identify products and business areas that warrant further investigation.
- Develop evidence-based business recommendations.

## 4. Tools

- Microsoft Excel: Data cleaning, exploratory analysis, formulas, and PivotTables.
- SQL: Data querying, aggregation, and business analysis.
- Power BI: Data visualization and dashboard development.
- Python: Supporting data inspection and exploratory analysis, where appropriate.

## 5. Dataset

The dataset contains retail transaction records, including order and shipping dates, customer information, geographic details, product categories, sales, quantity, discount, and profit.

The dataset will be examined for data-quality issues before conclusions are drawn.

## 6. Analytical Approach

1. Understand the dataset and define the business questions.
2. Inspect data types, missing values, duplicates, and potentially invalid records.
3. Prepare and validate the data.
4. Analyze sales, profit, discounts, and product performance.
5. Cross-check important findings across analytical tools.
6. Communicate findings and develop recommendations.

## 7. Key Findings

Findings will be documented after the analysis is completed and validated.

## 8. Business Recommendations

Recommendations will be based on the analytical results and will distinguish confirmed findings from areas requiring further investigation.

## 9. Limitations

The dataset may not contain all the information needed to explain business performance. For example, sales and profit figures alone may not reveal every underlying cost or operational factor.

The analysis will acknowledge these limitations when interpreting the results.
